\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Jesus, Thou art standing
\par Outside the fast-closed door,
\par In lowly patience waiting
\par To pass the thresold o'er.
\par Shame on us, Christian brothers,
\par His name and sign who bear,
\par O shame, thrice shame upon us,
\par To keep Him standing there!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O Jesus, Thou art knocking;
\par And lo, that hand is scarred,
\par And thorns Thy brow encircle,
\par And tears Thy face have married.
\par O love that passeth knowledge,
\par So patiently to wait!
\par O sin that hath no equal,
\par So fast to bar the gate!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Jesus, Thou art pleading
\par In accents meek and low,
\par I died for you, My children,
\par And will ye treat Me so?
\par O Lord,with shame and sorrow
\par We open now the door;
\par Dear Saviour, enter, enter,
\par And leave us nevermore.
\par                           Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

